    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0572" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg466"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tsui to Mr.
                            Wharton</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1891</hi>.</date>
                        (Received August 14.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have heretofore been under the necessity
                    of bringing your attention to the riotous proceedings of a band of lawless
                    people of the town of Vallejo, Cal., directed against certain peaceable and
                    law-abiding Chinese subjects, merchants of said town of Vallejo.</p>
                <p>It is now my duty to lay before you an official communication from the imperial
                    consul-general at San Francisco, containing a detailed account of the riotous
                    events referred to and of the losses and damages sustained by the Chinese
                    subjects therein named.</p>
                <p>In view of the statements made in said communication, if any further action of
                    the part of the National Government can, in your judgment, be taken to secure
                    the punishment of the guilty parties and protection of the Chinese subjects from
                    further violence and loss, it will be very gratifying to my Government.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsui Kwo Yin</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d422-a1.xml" xpointer="d422-a1"/>
            </div>
